Tutorial on how to Obtain the Parameters for Different Configurations of the M13 nanogenerator

This tutorial provides step-by-step instructions to guide users on how to:
1- Set up a simulation for the M13 nanogenerator in different configurations.
2- Run Finite Element Analysis (FEA) to obtain the resonance frequency and voltage output.
3- Integrate these parameters into the black box model used in this software tool.
While we are using COMSOL Multiphysics in this tutorial, this process can be replicated in other FEA tools such as ANSYS, Abaqus, or OpenFOAM.

Step 1: 	Setting Up the FEA Simulation in COMSOL Multiphysics:
	1.1: 	Open COMSOL Multiphysics and Create a New Model:
		Select “Model Wizard” —> 3D Component.
		Choose “Solid Mechanics” under the Physics tab.
		Add “Electrostatics” to account for piezoelectric coupling.

	1.2: 	Define the Geometry of the M13 nanogenerator:
		Create a desired geometry to represent the nanogenerator.

	1.3: 	Assign Material Properties:
		Use the following material properties from our previous publication (azarnoush2023) to model the M13 nanogenerator:
		Elastic Compliance Matrix [S] (in Pa⁻¹):
		[S] = [[0.2439, -0.0927, -0.2533, 0, 0, 0],
		[-0.0927, 0.2439, -0.2533, 0, 0, 0],
		[-0.0927, -0.0927, 0.6667, 0, 0, 0],
		[0, 0, 0, 0.6494, 0, 0],
		[0, 0, 0, 0, 0.6494, 0],
		[0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0.3366]] x 10⁻⁹

		Piezoelectric Coupling Matrix [d] (in V⁻¹):
		[d] = [[6.5, 12.1, 0, 0, 0, 0],
		[12.17, 6.5, 0, 0, 0, 0],
		[12.1, 12.1, 13.2, 0, 0, 0]] x 10⁻¹²

		Dielectric Constant (in F/m):
		ε = 22.577 x 10⁻¹² F/m

		Density (ρ):
		ρ = 833.88 kg/m³

	1.4:	Apply Boundary Conditions:
		Fix the boundaries conditions based on the desired configuration.
		Apply a mechanical force or ultrasonic wave stimulation to simulate the input.

Step 2: 	Run the analysis:
		Choose Eigenfrequency Study to calculate the natural resonance frequencies.
		Once you’ve identified the resonance frequencies from the Eigenfrequency Study, perform a Frequency Domain Study to calculate the output voltage for different ultrasonic inputs.

Step 2: 	Updating the Black Box Model in the Software Tool
		Export the voltage output data from COMSOL as a table.
		To integrate the new values into your black box model update the Voltage Lookup Table (nano_bubble/M13_Voltage_V3.xlsx) with the new data. 


References:
Azarnoush A, Dambri OA, Karatop EU, Makrakis D, Cherkaoui S. Simulation and Performance Evaluation of a Bio-Inspired Nanogenerator for Medical Applications. IEEE Trans Biomed Eng. 2023 Sep;70(9):2616-2623. doi: 10.1109/TBME.2023.3260200. Epub 2023 Aug 30. PMID: 37030752.
